# | msgid ""
# | "FreeRadio is an internet radio, podcast, and audio-book add-on for NVDA "
# | "that provides seamless access to thousands of internet radio stations via "
# | "the Radio Browser open directory, RSS/Atom podcast feeds, and the "
# | "libriVox + GETEM digital library for the visually impaired. It features a "
# | "fully accessible station browser with search, country filter, favourites "
# | "management, and per-station, per-podcast, and per-audio-book audio "
# | "profiles. Podcast episodes and audio book chapters resume automatically "
# | "from where you left off, with adjustable pitch-preserving playback speed. "
# | "Playback is handled by BASS, with support for volume control, audio "
# | "effects, output device selection, and simultaneous audio mirroring to a "
# | "second device. Additional features include instant and scheduled "
# | "recording, time-shift rewind of live radio, sleep and alarm timers, "
# | "automatic ICY metadata announcements, Shazam-based music recognition, and "
# | "a liked-songs log with lyrics lookup. All controls and shortcuts are "
# | "designed for NVDA accessibility."
#. Add-on description
#. Translators: Long description to be shown for this add-on
#: buildVars.py:19
msgid ""
"FreeRadio is an internet radio, podcast, audio-book, and local music add-on "
"for NVDA that provides seamless access to thousands of internet radio "
"stations via the Radio Browser open directory, RSS/Atom podcast feeds, the "
"libriVox + GETEM digital library for the visually impaired, and your own "
"local audio files and folders through its built-in jukebox. It features a "
"fully accessible station browser with search, country filter, favourites "
"management, and per-station, per-podcast, per-audio-book, and per-jukebox-"
"track audio profiles. Podcast episodes, audio book chapters, and jukebox "
"tracks resume automatically from where you left off - jukebox folders even "
"pick up on the last track you were playing - with adjustable pitch-"
"preserving playback speed and independent pitch-shift (semitone transpose). "
"Playback is handled by BASS, with support for volume control, audio effects, "
"output device selection, and simultaneous audio mirroring to a second "
"device. Additional features include instant and scheduled recording, time-"
"shift rewind of live radio, sleep and alarm timers, automatic ICY metadata "
"announcements, Shazam-based music recognition, and a liked-songs log with "
"lyrics lookup. All controls and shortcuts are designed for NVDA "
"accessibility."
msgstr ""
"FreeRadio è un’estensione per NVDA che permette di accedere a radio "
"Internet, podcast, audiolibri e musica locale. Offre un accesso senza "
"interruzioni a migliaia di stazioni radiofoniche tramite il database aperto "
"Radio Browser, i feed podcast RSS/Atom, la biblioteca digitale libriVox + "
"GETEM per non vedenti, e ai propri file e cartelle audio tramite il jukebox "
"integrato. Include un browser di stazioni completamente accessibile, con "
"funzionalità di ricerca, filtro per paese, gestione dei preferiti e profili "
"audio personalizzabili per ogni stazione, podcast, audiolibro e brano del "
"jukebox. Gli episodi dei podcast, i capitoli degli audiolibri e i brani del "
"jukebox riprendono automaticamente da dove si era interrotta la "
"riproduzione; le cartelle del jukebox ricordano persino l’ultimo brano "
"ascoltato. È possibile regolare la velocità di riproduzione mantenendo il "
"tono originale e applicare uno spostamento di semitoni indipendente. La "
"riproduzione è gestita da BASS e supporta il controllo del volume, gli "
"effetti audio, la selezione del dispositivo di uscita e lo specchiamento "
"audio simultaneo su un secondo dispositivo. Tra le funzionalità aggiuntive "
"figurano la registrazione istantanea e programmata, il riavvolgimento della "
"radio in diretta, timer per il sonno e sveglia, annunci automatici dei "
"metadati ICY, riconoscimento musicale basato su Shazam e un registro delle "
"canzoni preferite con ricerca dei testi. Tutti i comandi e i shortcut sono "
"progettati per garantire l’accessibilità con NVDA."

#. Brief changelog for this version
#. Translators: what's new content for the add-on version
#: buildVars.py:26
msgid ""
"\n"
"## Fixed\n"
"- **Wrong duration/bitrate/sample rate/channels for some MP3s** (e.g. "
"showing 12:44 instead of 4:46, mono instead of stereo, 32 kbps / 8 kHz "
"instead of the real values). Caused by a missing entry in the MPEG bitrate "
"table for Version 2/2.5 Layer III files (common for lower sample-rate MP3s), "
"which made frame detection fail and lock onto random bytes elsewhere in the "
"file.\n"
"- **VBR files could report the placeholder bitrate** of the dummy \"Xing\"/ "
"\"Info\"/\"VBRI\" header frame instead of the track's real average bitrate.\n"
"- **Files without an ID3v2 tag could be probed from the wrong byte offset**, "
"throwing off duration/bitrate/sample rate/channel detection.\n"
"## Added\n"
"- **Jukebox folders now resume from the last track played**, not always "
"track 1. The track index is remembered per folder (new "
"`jukebox_folder_positions.json`, alongside the existing `podcast_positions."
"json`) and updated every time a track starts playing as part of a folder "
"sequence - including automatic advance while the dialog is closed. Cleared "
"once the folder is played through to its last track, so it starts over next "
"time; also cleared if the folder is removed from the jukebox library.\n"
"- An explicit selection already made in the tracks list still wins over the "
"remembered position - this only kicks in when nothing's selected.\n"
"- Within-track resume position (the existing per-file feature) applies on "
"top of this automatically, so the resumed track picks up mid-song too.\n"
"## Changed\n"
"- Playing a folder (or a single file) now updates the tracks list's "
"selection to the track that actually starts playing, without moving keyboard "
"focus there.\n"
"## Added\n"
"- The tracks list selection now also follows the playing track when it "
"changes on its own: a track finishing and auto-advancing to the next one, or "
"a Ctrl+Win+J/K seek crossing into a different track. Only updates if the "
"folder being advanced is the one currently shown in the tracks list; never "
"moves keyboard focus.\n"
"## Fixed\n"
"- Playing a jukebox track (single file or folder) no longer requires an "
"internet connection. The connectivity check in `_play_station()` now skips "
"jukebox tracks (`media_kind == \"jukebox\"`), since they're local files and "
"never touch the network.\n"
"## Fixed\n"
"- Time-shift (rewind) now works on stations that use a \"redirect\" style "
"address, such as many TuneIn stations. Previously, time-shift would try to "
"reconnect over and over without ever actually buffering anything, so rewind "
"wasn't available on those stations - even though normal playback worked "
"fine. Regular listening was never affected.\n"
msgstr ""

